  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade QUISP Prog (MTTI) - Monitoring Support to QUISP</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Trade QUISP Prog (MTTI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">QUISP &#xe4;r ett fem&#xe5;rigt program under den Ugandiska regeringen med      uppgift att fr&#xe4;mja anv&#xe4;ndningen av standarder och                     kvalitetsinfrastruktur. M&#xe5;let &#xe4;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra konkurrenskraften f&#xf6;r  ugandiska produkter, processer och tj&#xe4;nsteleveranssystem p&#xe5; inhemska, regionala och internationella marknader. Programmet innefattar bland  annat en omarbetning av det r&#xe4;ttsliga ramverket i Uganda, utveckling.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The QUISP is a 5 yr GoU programme with the goal to promote the use of standards and quality infrastructure to improve the competitiveness   of Ugandan products, processes and service delivery systems in        domestic, regional and international markets. it entails a review of  the legal and regulatory framework, development of a coordinaition    mechanism and a communication stragegy amongst others.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ministry of Tourism, Trade and instustry (MTTI) has implemented a five-year programme: Quality infrastructure and standards programme. The programme seeks to develop a market driven, holistic and coordinated insitutional framework for the Uganda Quality infrastructure and standards framework; which supports trade, industry, health, safety, consumer protection and a sustainable environment while at the same time promoting use of best practices in the production and service sectors.
The programme commenced in 2010 with the support of Sida and was set to close in December 2014. However, an extension was given until March 2017.
The overall objective is to promote the use standards and quality infrastructure so as to improve the competitiveness of Ugandand products, processes and service delivery systems in domestic, regional and international markets.
The following goals have formed implementation of the programme:
- To develop a policy for standardization and review strategies for policy implementation.
- To develop a comprehensive and effective legal framework for the implementation of standardization.
- To establish an effective coordination mechanism with clearly defined mandates and responsibilities for the different actors in the standards and quality area.
- to rationalize the institutional set up of service providers for standards development, confirmity assessment and measurement services.
- to enhance public awareness on standards and quality products and best practices.</narrative>
  </description>
